# Consult submodule rules first

This repo vendors shared trees as git submodules (`jfrog-helm-values`,
`scripts-general-util`, …). Each submodule owns conventions for its
paths. Project-wide rules live here (`ps-customer-template`) and sync
to customer clones.

Before a change that spans this repo and a submodule (compose labels
plus `helm/` symlinks, sizing, OpenShift flavor, shared scripts):

1. Read that submodule's `.cursor/rules/` (and README / AGENTS.md).
2. Follow those rules inside the submodule. Do not copy or restate
   them in this repo.
3. Keep customer-repo rules to glue only: `helm/` stack, site files,
   CI, `.envrc`.

```text
# BAD
Add compose label naming to this repo's .cursor/rules and invent a
label that mixes network policy with image pins.

# GOOD
Read jfrog-helm-values/.cursor/rules/single-concern-labels.mdc,
add one label in the submodule, then symlink it from helm/.
```
